      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T10:33:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Only server-authentication is read from tls-client-parameters here. client-identity, hello-params and keepalives are silently dropped, so a configured client certificate or a TLS 1.3/cipher restriction just disappears when switching from the TLS case to Quic. Could we throw UnsupportedConfigurationException when any of them is present (as is done for raw public keys), or wire client-identity into QuicSslContextBuilder.keyManager()?",
      "revId": "bfa61598d880ed79eebcb62ec529e8d9eb49681b",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
